{
  "sheet": "effects",
  "about": "Visual effect ids used by skills.effect/vfx/extra. Deadlock's particle systems (.vpcf) are never read or copied: visuals reuse Risk of Rain 2's own effect prefabs and materials (Addressables keys checked against the installed catalog.json) or are built by our own code in Unity (kind custom: plugin/Runtime/Vfx.cs, made to look like Deadlock). kind: tracer (bullet line muzzle->hit), impact (one-shot at a point, scaled by radius when scaleWithRadius), ghost (attached visual that follows a mod-simulated projectile), orb (RoR2 OrbManager lightning orb), trail (vanilla DamageTrail fire trail), attachment (a RoR2 NetworkedBodyAttachment put on the hero), ward (a RoR2 BuffWard placed on the ground), material (a RoR2 material our custom visuals are drawn with), custom (built by Vfx.cs; addressable none), none. prop: a Deadlock model the extractor reads from the player's install as a plain mesh (addressable = its vmdl path; extractor 1.5.0+), drawn by Vfx with our own materials; a prop that could not be read falls back to a simple shape. meshes / clips (props only, extractor 1.6.0+): the model's meshes to read (none = all) and the clips to read with its skeleton (none = a still mesh): Rat King's rat runs and leaps, his banner's sewer rises out of the ground. tint: a RoR2 prefab (tracer, impact) recoloured to this colour (#RRGGBB) as our own copy, registered as an effect of the mod (Fx.Prefab); its materials' colour ramps are redrawn in it (Seven's yellow Shock Rifle tracer), none = as RoR2 has it.",
  "columns": [
    "id",
    "kind",
    "addressable",
    "scaleWithRadius",
    "meshes",
    "clips",
    "tint",
    "notes"
  ],
